# Improvement measurement and taxonomy promotion
## 1. Why this procedure exists
The skill's gates are all negative: edit-rate caps, two overediting checks, and
content-damage audits. They limit damage without measuring improvement. An
edit-rate gate does not itself provide an improvement metric.
`content-fidelity-auditor` correctly excludes style, rhythm, and naturalness
assessment. Combining content preservation and quality judgment in one role
would compromise both.
No automated measurement exists today. Use a recording procedure that makes
unfilled human evaluation visible rather than pretending it is automated.
## 2. Blinded paired comparison
### Procedure
1. Prepare original A and edited B. Remove filenames, headers, revision history,
and every other marker identifying the edited version.
2. Present the versions in random order, randomized independently for each pair.
3. Have the evaluator answer three questions without knowing which was edited.
4. Reveal labels after receiving the answers and add one row to the record.
### Three questions
| Question | Ask | Answer format |
|---|---|---|
| Q1 | Which version sounds human-written? | A / B / 구분 불가 |
| Q2 | Which version fits this genre? | A / B / 차이 없음 |
| Q3 | Does any content seem changed? | 있음(location) / 없음 |
Q2 prevents genre drift from appearing as improvement in Q1. More colloquial
wording can score better on Q1 while making a procurement proposal worse.
A Q3 answer of `있음` excludes the pair from quality comparison and sends it to
the delta audit in `register-invariants.md`. Comparing style after content has
changed is not a valid comparison.
### Record
| Field | Convention |
|---|---|
| `run_id` | `YYYY-MM-DD-NNN` generated by pipeline Phase 0 |
| `제시순서` | `AB` or `BA` |
| `평가자` | Identifier only; no name |
| `Q1` `Q2` `Q3` | Use the answer formats above |
| `블라인드` | `유지` or `깨짐` |
| `사유` | Only when blinding breaks |
Exclude pairs with broken blinding and retain the reason. Accumulated reasons
identify defects in the presentation procedure.
### Decision
- Make no judgment with fewer than 5 valid pairs. Insufficient samples are not a result.
- With at least 5 valid pairs, reconsider that run's recipe if Q1 preference for B is below 60%.
- If B preference is lower on Q2 than Q1, treat it as an overediting signal and inspect genre rules first.
## 3. Taxonomy promotion: v1 to v2
Observation alone does not qualify a new pattern for promotion.
| Stage | Condition | Output |
|---|---|---|
| Observation | Found in actual input | Register a candidate without a grade |
| v1 candidate | Reproduced in at least 2 distinct tasks | Draft rule, `class: HOLISTIC` |
| v1 | Controls confirm human authors rarely use it | Assign severity and enter the taxonomy |
| v2 promotion | Populate surface forms or metrics in machine fields | `class: ANCHORED` or `COMPUTED` |
The substantive promotion criterion is whether a machine can count rule firings.
If it cannot, retain `HOLISTIC` and record that limitation in the evidence grade.
Never promote a rule to `ANCHORED` without corpus validation.
Apply the table in reverse for demotion. Repeated runs with 0 positives require
lowering the grade and recording why. Never reclaim the number; historical
comparison depends on it.
## 4. Field outcomes
Procurement mode records outcomes separately from style improvement.
`outcomes.jsonl` has one project per line; append a row in pipeline Phase 5.
- Keep the `run_id` generated in Phase 0.
- `결과` accepts only `수주`, `탈락`, or `미정`.
- Copy `cat` directly from detection output's `category_summary`. Working folders
may be removed, but these 20–30 bytes remain available for comparison.
At 10 records, calculate correlations between K–O rule-firing frequencies and
outcomes, then reassess severity. Until then, K–O S1 grades are `잠정`.
`tests/test_outcomes_schema.js` checks the schema.
## 5. Re-audit measurement code
When a surface-matching error appears in one rule, recheck every rule for the
same error class. Fixing only the observed instance leaves discovery accidental.
`scripts/audit_measures.js` checks five axes: dead surface forms, unreachable
alternatives, unmeasured fields, unmeasured metrics, and overlapping surface forms.
Re-audit results from 2026-09-02:
| Item | Declared | Measured |
|---|---|---|
| ANCHORED | 27 | 26 |
| COMPUTED | 4 | 4 |
The one-rule gap is `C-10`. Its line-start anchor cannot match quoted examples
inside the rule section; it fires only on actual input heading lines. The rule
therefore records a `- 재감사:` exemption reason. Exemptions without reasons are
invalid; overly short reasons are reported as defects rather than exemptions.
The re-audit measures gaps between declarations and observations. It is not a
rule-passing tool. If adding exemption prose is the only way to reach 0, the
measurement has no value. Reasons therefore remain in rule bodies and visible diffs.
